    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`plan_extraction` is implemented in `solution.py` and follows all seven rules in `spec.md`. The 28 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass. I haven't seen the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit reports, because the only command I could run was the pytest one.\n\nThe logic is split into two small helpers, one for the raw-name checks and one for normalisation, so each function stays simple. The tests cover:\n- normalisation and ordinary dotted names like `..a`;\n- every unsafe-path case;\n- directory entries;\n- case-insensitive duplicates;\n- the root destination;\n- the rule that no partial plan is returned.\n\nOne test of mine was wrong at first. It treated `a:` as an ordinary name, but the spec makes a letter followed by `:` a drive prefix. I fixed the test, not the implementation.",
